{"availability":"available","full":"jjmginon/coffeescript-cafe","name":"coffeescript-cafe","description":"CoffeeScript Café is a responsive multi‑page website redesigned in 2026 with original café‑themed content to demonstrate accessibility, performance, and modern front‑end design practices. The project was originally inspired by Dave Gray’s HTML/CSS tutorials, but has since evolved into a fully independent showcase of front‑end craftsmanship.","category":"Design","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-09-16T14:50:49Z","updated":"2026-10-09T03:55:48Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://coffeescript-cafe.netlify.app/","topics":["css3","dave-gray","html5","javascript","responsive-design","semantic-html"],"demo":"https://coffeescript-cafe.netlify.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:08:04.769Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T11:08:04.769Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T11:08:04.769Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:08:04.769Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["CoffeeScript Café is a fictional coffee shop website redesigned in 2026 with a modern design system, accessibility‑first structure, and performance‑optimized styling. Originally inspired by beginner tutorials, the project has since evolved into a fully independent showcase of front‑end craftsmanship — blending semantic HTML, responsive CSS, and clean JavaScript into a cohesive user experience."],"features":["Accessibility‑first design","Semantic elements, descriptive alt text, ARIA‑friendly structure, and focus styles for keyboard users.","Grid and flexbox for adaptive sections, fluid typography, and media queries for small and large screens.","CSS variables, dark‑mode support, scroll‑driven animations, and component‑based class naming.","Coffee‑and‑code themed menu items (Java Coffee, ByteBlend Frappe, BubbleSort Milk Tea), playful trivia, and thematic copywriting."],"sourceUrl":"https://g